WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.780 line:62%,end
Prior to having the procedure done,

2
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.240
I had been having some lower back pain

3
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.770
and it started radiating into my hips

4
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:32.790
and then I started having like a burning pain

5
00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:35.350
and it was about the middle of my butt cheek

6
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.890
but it went down into the bend of my knee

7
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:44.270
and it was like a shooting, burning,
constant fire, like on fire all the time.

8
00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.850 line:62%,end
It was really difficult for me to walk.

9
00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:51.230 line:62%,end
I had to kind of limp around and there
were some days I got out of bed,

10
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.050 line:62%,end
I didn't think I was going to be
able to walk. It was rough.

11
00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.340 line:62%,end
Now, I'd had several procedures to my back,
so I was used to back pain anyways,

12
00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.680 line:62%,end
but this was above and beyond
the normal aches and pains.

13
00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:07.550 line:62%,end
I've put up with it for about five years,

14
00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.210
and then I decided to come
back to Dr. Rutledge.

15
00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.990
I hadn't been here for a little while,

16
00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:19.010
and talked to him about what was going
on because my fear was that I was going

17
00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:22.330
to have to have another fusion done,
that it was a disc that was involved

18
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:27.650
and I've been through that before
and it was just a horrible thing.

19
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.110 line:62%,end
I really didn't want to have to go
through another back surgery, you know.

20
00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.550 line:62%,end
I talked to Dr. Rutledge and he said, well,

21
00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:41.190
I want to check your sacroiliac
joints, your SI joints

22
00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.770
and see if that's not the problem.

23
00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.170
And I thought, well,
that sounds kind of crazy,

24
00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.090
but yeah, sure, we'll check it out, you know.

25
00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:52.310
And so the way they did that
was they did some injections

26
00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:57.420
and just kind of numbed the areas
to see if that was effective

27
00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.510
and it lasted for maybe a couple of hours,
but it felt great, you know.

28
00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:04.890
So I said, yeah, that that really helped.

29
00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.330
I can't believe how much
it made me feel better.

30
00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:11.270 line:62%,end
So we went ahead and did
the procedures one side at a time.

31
00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:16.410 line:62%,end
And the first side that he did was
the worst side with the burning pain.

32
00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.720 line:62%,end
The next day, the day after I had the surgery
and all the numbness and anesthesia wore off.

33
00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:28.740
I was actually able to walk without
limping on that leg and it felt so good.

34
00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:32.720
I didn't have the burning pain
anymore. I didn't have hip pain.

35
00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.640
My lower back felt better on that
side. It was just a life changer.

36
00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.200
And so I was so excited about
having the other side done.

37
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.810
And when I got that side done,
then it alleviated all my pain.

38
00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:52.330
I have no more burning pain. I have no more
lower back pain. I have no more hip pain,

39
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.450
now I have a little bit
of an ache here and there,

40
00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.530
but you know that's just
a normal thing for me,

41
00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:02.550
but not like it was. I mean it
wasn't an excruciating pain.

42
00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.850
This pain took so much away from me in life.

43
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:09.110
My quality of life was was deteriorated.

44
00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.370
I wasn't able to do the things that I enjoyed.

45
00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:16.650
I loved to go camping and fishing
and gardening and just walking my dog

46
00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:20.790
And those things were so difficult
that I just couldn't do them anymore.

47
00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.710
And after the surgery, about a week after
the surgery, I took my dog for a walk

48
00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:28.550
and I walked her for a mile
around the block, you know.

49
00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:33.130
And I was able to walk across the grocery
store without hobbling on the cart.

50
00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:38.190
And I was able to start exercising
again and I've lost some weight.

51
00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:42.010
It's just improved my quality
of health in general.

52
00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:46.790
I was able to start going camping
and fishing. I have a big garden.

53
00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.310
I've been able to do things
that I wasn't able to do before.

54
00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:54.770
And the surgery was just life
changing. It was so amazing.

55
00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:58.430
I just couldn't believe it.
You know, to be this pain-free,

56
00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:02.540
I even stopped taking narcotic
medication. I no longer need it.
